# 28. Codex Implementation Instructions

This work contains both mechanical implementation work and architectural boundaries reserved for manual design.

Codex should implement only the well-defined portions below.

## 28.1 Before changing code

First inspect the existing tree and identify:

1. current FacetOS IDL conventions;
2. interface naming conventions;
3. UUID conventions;
4. enum conventions;
5. string representation and bounds;
6. getter/setter conventions;
7. interface-return/out-parameter conventions;
8. error/result conventions;
9. current configuration parser structures;
10. portable configuration resolution structures;
11. dominit0 materialisation;
12. build integration for generated interfaces;
13. existing tests for configuration parsing and validation.

Follow existing conventions.

Do not introduce a second architectural style.

