# 32. Ambiguity Rule

If implementation reaches a point where completing the requested work requires an architectural choice not specified here:

> Do not invent the architecture.

Instead:

1. isolate the unresolved boundary;
2. leave a concise TODO describing exactly what is missing;
3. continue implementing independent well-defined portions;
4. report the unresolved decision at completion.

Do not replace an unresolved architectural question with a speculative abstraction.

