# 33. Completion Behaviour

Codex must make concrete code changes.

Do not stop merely to explain the implementation plan or announce that implementation is beginning.

After changing the code:

1. run the relevant generator;
2. run configuration/parser tests;
3. run relevant interface tests;
4. run the build;
5. fix regressions caused by the changes;
6. distinguish pre-existing failures from new failures.

At completion report:

* files added;
* files modified;
* configuration structures added or changed;
* IDL interfaces/enums added;
* validation rules implemented;
* tests added;
* commands/tests/builds run and their results;
* unresolved architectural boundaries deliberately left for manual implementation.

The task is complete only after implementation and validation, or after reaching a genuine architectural blocker that prevents further independent work.

